<title>FRANCE: BP Lavera cuts runs due to one-day strike.</title>
<headline>BP Lavera cuts runs due to one-day strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>BP France cut operations at its Lavera refinery near Marseille to a minimum safe level on Tuesday as workers joined a one-day national protest over oil industry job cuts, an official at the plant said.</p>
<p>Refinery managers slowed the plant down to its minimum safe level after 90 percent of shift workers went on strike at 0400 GMT, the official said.</p>
<p>The CGT union said all shift workers took part.</p>
<p>The strike was expected to last 24 hours.</p>
<p>Unions have called the action over oil industry plans to cut an estimated 1,500 refining jobs over the next year.</p>
</text>
